  "track.coroutines.m.builders.s.settingsFailConc.explain": "settings throws at {t} ms. Because both jobs are children of `coroutineScope`, the scope is cancelled and the still-running profile job is cancelled too.",
  "track.coroutines.m.builders.s.combineConc.explain": "Both jobs are done, so the parent resumes, combines the results and completes. The total is about {p} ms: the longer job, not the sum.",
  "track.coroutines.m.builders.co.try": "Turn on \"Run concurrently\", then add \"settings throws\" and see whether profile still finishes.",
  "track.coroutines.m.builders.co.seq": "Sequential by default: writing two suspend calls one after another does not make them run together. [[src:kt-composing]]",
  "track.coroutines.m.builders.co.await": "`async` returns `Deferred<T>`; you get the result with `await()`. Use `async` when you really need concurrency and a return value; if you need no result, `launch` is enough. [[src:kt-composing]]",
  "track.coroutines.m.builders.co.structured": "If something goes wrong inside `concurrentSum` and it throws, all the coroutines launched in its scope are cancelled. [[src:kt-composing]]",
  "track.coroutines.m.builders.co.conc": "Concurrency is not automatically better in every case: it trades waiting time for complexity around cancellation and failure.",
