  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.title": "Cancellation is cooperative",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.overview": "A coroutine does 5 units of work, 100 ms each (assumed). You choose when to cancel it, or set a timeout, and whether the code checks for cancellation, swallows `CancellationException`, or cleans up in `finally`.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.wrapup": "Cancellation is only a request: the coroutine stops when it cooperates (suspends or checks for cancellation). Code that never checks keeps running; catching `CancellationException` without rethrowing defeats cancellation; a suspend function in `finally` needs `NonCancellable` to run.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.simp.1": "Each unit of 100 ms and the check at the end of each unit are illustrative assumptions. For timeouts, the model assumes the code checks for cancellation.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.simp.2": "Swallowing `CancellationException` is simplified: the model only shows that execution continues, not every consequence for the Job state.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ctl.hint": "Each change recomputes the scenario from the start.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ctl.mode": "What stops it",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ctl.mode.cancel": "cancel() from outside",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ctl.mode.timeout": "withTimeout(250 ms)",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ctl.mode.timeoutNull": "withTimeoutOrNull(250 ms)",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ctl.coop": "Code checks for cancellation (ensureActive)",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ctl.at": "Cancel during unit",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ctl.at.n": "unit {n}",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ctl.swallow": "Catch and swallow CancellationException (wrong)",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ctl.fin": "Cleanup in finally",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ctl.fin.none": "none",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ctl.fin.plain": "a plain suspend call",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.ctl.fin.nc": "withContext(NonCancellable)",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.diagramTitle": "The caller, the coroutine and the cleanup block",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.diagramDesc": "The caller on the left sends the cancellation request to the coroutine; the coroutine may run the cleanup block below",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.n.caller": "The cancel() caller",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.n.job": "Coroutine",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.n.cleanup": "The finally block",
